// A freestanding program with NOTHING in it. The point is what must not be in the image.
//
// `onClassLoad` hooks are called from the entry, and that call is what keeps a hook alive: it is
// emitted before dead-stripping, so a prelude class nobody touches stops being dead the moment the
// entry calls it. The prelude's `Test` is the only class in it with a hook, its body assigns two
// static `String`s, and a String store lowers to `__polaron_str_copy` / `__polaron_str_free` -- symbols
// no bare-metal image has.
//
// The failure was not a wrong answer. It was a LINK error in somebody else's kernel naming two
// symbols they never wrote, on a program whose whole source is these eleven lines.
program FreestandingNoPreludeHooks freestanding;

public bundle Kernel {
    public namespace Boot {
        public class Main {
            public static method main(string[] args) returns void { return; }
        }
    }
}
